								<p class="newsTitle">
									Soldier will be reforming. - 
									2/24/2005 2:16:02 PM
								</p>
								<div class="newsBody">
									<p>With PB's downfall and reforming under Rapture I have come to realize that we stand no chance in competing with them for recruits. We are losing people and the guild will not last much longer so I ask that you listen to the next paragraph with that in mind.<br /><br />Later today I will be typing in /gdisband. I will then reform the guild with only members who wish to be in a small friends only guild. I ask those of you that would like to continue raiding and advancing our servers renown to ask Rapture for an interview. I wish you all well and good luck in the future.<br /><br />VileSin</p>
								</div>
							</td>
	</tr><tr>
		<td>
								<div class="newsSeperator">&nbsp;</div>
							</td>
	</tr><tr>
		<td class="grid_col2" align="Center">
								<p class="newsTitle">
									Coming Changes - 
									2/20/2005 11:13:34 AM
								</p>
								<div class="newsBody">
									As of last night, Saturday, February 19 I (VileSin) have been placed in charge of the guild. Most of you know me and you know I want the guild to succeed above all else. With this change in leadership will be a shakedown of the guild. We will be reviewing our rules and changing whats necessary and adding a few more officers.<br /><br />That being said you will also notice we have a lot more members now than we did even one week ago. Welcome them to Soldier and help each other out when you can. There's not much to do when you hit 60 besides raiding and you need as many people as you can for that so help each other out.<br /><br />Ziga is also our recruiting officer now. If you have someone you think would make an excellent addition to Soldier refer them to him. They may have to wait or send him mail in game due to his late hours but they will be contacted.<br /><br />Have fun and see you in game!
								</div>
							</td>
	</tr><tr>
